This week we finally got to meet with Nadia, which was helpful since we missed her the last time we went to her studio. 
She shared the music for the project with us, but she's not sure yet if we will continue with it. 
She mentioned that she might want to use a poem instead. To show us what she meant, she showed us samples of her work that had hidden poems
in them. I thought this was interesting because it connects to her ceramic work in a more personal way, 
and it could change the direction of the sound part of the project.
She also proposed making a mini piece for us as a sample.
This would be really useful because it would give us something real to test with instead of only working from ideas.
Nadia gave us feedback on our design too. The main point was that she wants the scanner to be wireless.
She also felt that the design for the scanner was too clunky and said she preferred a tube shape. 
This means we will need to rethink part of our design so it fits better with what she has in mind.
Overall, the meeting went well, and we now have a lot of feedback to work with.
Some of our questions from before were answered, but there are still decisions to make, 
like whether we go with the music or the poem. Next, we have to figure out how we're going to approach the work with the time we have left. 
I think it will be important for the team to divide the tasks clearly and decide what is realistic to finish.
